# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Declutter AI — API keys for the multi-provider XAI fallback chain
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file:   cp .env.example .env
#   2. Paste your keys below (no quotes needed)
#   3. Start the backend:  python run.py
#      run.py calls load_dotenv() automatically, so the keys are picked up.
#
# You do NOT need all keys — set the ones you have.
# The chain tries providers in order and skips any with a missing key.
# Order (cheapest / most generous free tier first):
#   1  Groq llama-3.3-70b-versatile    ← GROQ_API_KEY   (free tier)
#   2  Gemini 2.0 Flash                ← GOOGLE_API_KEY
#   3  Gemini 1.5 Flash                ← GOOGLE_API_KEY  (same key)
#   4  Mistral Small                   ← MISTRAL_API_KEY
#   5  DeepSeek Chat                   ← DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
#   6  Cohere Command-R+               ← COHERE_API_KEY
#   7  Claude Haiku                    ← ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#   8  GPT-4o Mini                     ← OPENAI_API_KEY
#   9  Claude Sonnet                   ← ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (same key)
#  10  GPT-4o                          ← OPENAI_API_KEY   (same key)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1. Groq  — https://console.groq.com/keys
#    Free tier · 30 req/min · llama-3.3-70b-versatile
GROQ_API_KEY= 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

# 2+3. Google AI Studio  — https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
#    Gemini 2.0 Flash and Gemini 1.5 Flash share the same key
